# Internal planning/operating docs stay local; judge-facing READMEs ship.
*.md
!/README.md
!/subgraph/README.md
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
artifacts/
**/artifacts/
out/
**/out/
cache/
**/cache/
broadcast/
**/broadcast/
deployments/
**/deployments/
coverage/
**/coverage/
.env*
!.env.example

# Vendored aqua/ and swap-vm/ upstream checkouts: only the subset actually
# needed to build+test Rook's contracts is tracked (verified via a clean-
# checkout rebuild, see HANDOFF.md open item 3). These are the upstream
# repos' own tooling/docs/unrelated test suites — never required, and
# committing them would bloat history for no benefit. If a future test
# genuinely needs one of these, `git add -f <path>` it deliberately.
aqua/.editorconfig
aqua/.env.example
aqua/.gas-snapshot
aqua/.github/
aqua/.gitignore
aqua/.npmrc
aqua/.yarnrc.yml
aqua/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
aqua/config/
aqua/docs/
aqua/examples/
aqua/foundry.lock
aqua/test/
swap-vm/.cursor/
swap-vm/.editorconfig
swap-vm/.env.example
swap-vm/.gas-snapshot
swap-vm/.github/
swap-vm/.gitignore
swap-vm/.npmrc
swap-vm/.yarnrc.yml
swap-vm/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
swap-vm/config/
swap-vm/docs/
swap-vm/ignition/
swap-vm/mocks/
swap-vm/scope.txt
swap-vm/snapshots/
swap-vm/test/
